From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:49:16 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: isp: set up the temporal filter per sensor as
 macOS does

On the H17 interface macOS does not start the ISP's temporal noise filter
the same way for every sensor. For the IMX958 (J616s) it sends a longer
start record, (1, 0, 0), then turns high-strength filtering and band 0
modulation off and sets the band 0 strength thresholds to 120 and 100 in
1/256 steps, before the motion history and the enable. For the IMX558
(J700) it starts nothing: it disables the filter and stops the motion
history and the filter, since the firmware keeps that state between
streams. These values come from Daybreak's reading of the macOS 27.0
camera stack.

Linux sent the short start with the apple,temporal-filter value on every
sensor, 1 on the J700. On the Neo, starting the filter with 0 instead of
1 already leaves about 13% less luma noise and 18% less chroma noise on a
still scene.

Keep the per-sensor choice next to the setfile of each sensor and leave
every other sensor on the original sequence.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(cherry picked from commit 7f9611314715fbebe4dfed79e2b60225273a30e8)
---
